  "worked_solution": "After shifting a linear system, the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors remain unchanged.\n\nThus, the matrix $B$ in the shifted system has the same eigenvectors as the system's matrix in the original coordinates. These eigenvectors are ${w}_{1}$ and ${w}_{2},$ or any nonzero vectors that are parallel to them.\n\nAmong the given options, the only vector that is nonzero and is guaranteed to be parallel to either ${w}_{1}$ or ${w}_{2}$ is the vector $5{w}_{1}.$",
